  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The M with a wall pass – pass, return and shoot",
  "description": "A development of the M. One line in each corner at one end and a cone on each side further out towards the middle. A runs down along the boards, rounds their cone and gets the pass from B in the other corner. A plays it straight back to B and keeps going straight in towards goal. B plays another first-time pass and A shoots first time from the slot – a backhand works well, since the goal is close. Then B runs round the cone on their side and does the same with line A.\n\nMake sure the players really run out and round the cone. Otherwise they end up too close to goal, the drill loses pace and it gets crowded. Rotation: after the shot, join the other line. Variant: let A receive and fake past an imagined defender before the shot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Run all the way round the cone – shortcuts kill the tempo."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The return pass should be first time, firm and without bounce."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep going straight in towards goal after the one-two, not out to the boards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Try a backhand shot – the distance is short."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
